# case: struct_literal_bare_end
# decision: accidental (REJECT)
# anchor: the canonical struct-literal body (grammar.md §4.5
#         `struct_literal = ... '{' field_init_list '}'`) has no `end`
#         form. In the seed, `end` followed by a non-continuation token is
#         a block terminator via at_kw_end_as_terminator (parser.ml:243-253,
#         used in parse_struct_literal:2586): `S { end }` closes the field
#         list at `end` (the seed also has an end-terminated literal form,
#         `Name { ... end`, so the terminator is consumed) and leaves the
#         `}` stray, which the seed reports (E1100). The kernel's 155f72d
#         soft-name widening accepted `end` as a shorthand field here; the
#         kernel now breaks on the terminator `end` and keeps the
#         diagnostic, matching the seed.
struct S
  x: Int
end

def struct_literal_bare_end() -> Int
  S { end }
end
